From 2b320049a5df8e62e1b3ee70f53304d6d55a15e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:57:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep CED boundary normalization local and select residual
 rows before gather

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Integration base: candidate-36 at 6d4e49d1cdbb6513819e47145e0e52fdab327b6b.

The boundary needs every normalized row for global KV construction, but
only selected replay rows of the four-stream residual carry. Normalize
local SP rows, gather the global KV input and exchange compact carry slots.
Keep the full-carry path for dense selections whose slots would cost more.

Quality: retain the native weights, projections, replay selection and
rank-order arithmetic. Integer ownership selection introduces no floating
reduction and preserves signed zero and nonfinite payloads.

Tests: 122 CPU tests passed, one GPU-only test skipped; full base series
reapplies to the recorded tree. Added GPU mapping/graph cases are pending
hardware qualification. No measured serving-throughput gain is claimed.
Upstream status: experimental source-fork review; not proposed for promotion.
